=== Word formation ===

Maroniko has productive derivational processes:

* Reduplication (from Imo): intensifies meaning or indicates plurality
*: {{lang|bic|kúmi-kúmi}} — "eating" (activity), "plenty of food"

* Compounding: combines lexical roots
*: {{lang|bic|omí-nla}} — "big person", "adult" (omí + nla)
*: {{lang|bic|ile-kimì}} — "workhouse", "factory" (ile + kimì)

* Suffixation:
*: {{lang|bic|-nan}} — plural: {{lang|bic|àwọn-nan}} "those ones"
*: {{lang|bic|-ya}} — feminine (rare): {{lang|bic|omí-ya}} "woman"

== Writing system ==

Maroniko uses the [[W:Latin script|Mesogean alphabet]] with additional characters for Imo-derived sounds. The standardized orthography, adopted by the [[Academia de Maroniko]] in 1912, represents a compromise between phonetic representation and etymological preservation.

=== Orthographic conventions ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Letter !! IPA !! Example
|-
| c || /tʃ/ || {{lang|bic|cà}} ['tʃa] "to do"
|-
| j || /dʒ/ || {{lang|bic|jà}} [dʒa] "to be"
|-
| x || /ʃ/ || {{lang|bic|xà}} [ʃa] "to share"
|-
| z || /z/ || {{lang|bic|zá}} [za] "thing"
|-
| ñ || /ɲ/ || {{lang|bic|ñà}} [ɲa] "mother"
|-
| h || /h/ || {{lang|bic|hà}} [ha] "to take"
|-
| ḥ || /ħ/ || {{lang|bic|ḥà}} [ħa] (in Bayani/Imfezzan-derived words only)
|-
| kh || /x/ || {{lang|bic|khà}} [xa] (in Imfezzan loanwords)
|-
| gb || /ɡb/ || {{lang|bic|gbà}} [ɡba] "to break" (Imo-derived)
|-
| kp || /kp/ || {{lang|bic|kpà}} [kpa] (Imo-derived)
|}

Nasal vowels are indicated with a following -n or by tilde in standardized spelling:
* {{lang|bic|ãwã}} or {{lang|bic|anwa}} — "we"
* {{lang|bic|ẽ́}} or {{lang|bic|en}} — "song"

Accent marks indicate irregular stress or, in some cases, vowel quality distinctions from Imo substrate:
* {{lang|bic|ká-fe}} — "coffee" (stress on first syllable)
* {{lang|bic|èmi}} — "I" (low tone vowel from Imo)

